From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:59:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/86] Markdown preview: Source, Preview and Split views

Markdown files (.md, .markdown, .mdown, .mkd, .mkdn) get three views per
tab: Source (the editor), Preview (rendered, read-only) and Split (editor
and preview side by side). The setting "Open Markdown files in" picks the
view a file opens in (default Preview); an empty file opens in Source.

Switch with the header bar buttons, the View menu, Ctrl+Shift+V (Preview
and Source) and Ctrl+Alt+V (Split and Source). The preview uses the
libcosmic markdown widget styled from the COSMIC theme, parses only while
visible, and reparses 150 ms after the last edit or after a reload.

Links: http, https and mailto open in the default app; local text files
open in the editor; local images, audio, video and PDFs open in the
default app; anything else, including other schemes, executables and
desktop files, is ignored so a click never runs anything. Local images
show inline, remote ones as their alt text.

